WEBVTT

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.540
My passionate idol activities,

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:06.620
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.080
Our audition from the other day was recorded

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.490
and uploaded to Starlight Academy's website.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:15.720
Wow.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.980
You might even have a fan or two now.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.700
Really? Ah, hang on!

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.020
During this audition, didn't I...

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.920
Why does this part have to be uploaded too?!

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.760
This is the kind of footage that has to be preserved for all eternity.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.980
It's like a kind of communication with your fans, and part of your highlight reel.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.680
Above all else, it's so that fans can feel close to their idols.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:41.440
There's no way someone would become my fan from seeing this!

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:54.140
Hoshimiya Ichigo-chan...

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.370
Hi, signalize!

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:18.750
The answer lies on the other side of the sky

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:18.750
kotae wa motto takai sora no kanata

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:20.640
No, that's wrong

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:20.640
iie chigau yo

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:26.020
I can see with my eyes that it's at the end of the Earth

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:26.020
boku no me ni mo mieta chi no hate

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.810
Do that signalize!

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:32.990
Something's starting to bubble up

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:32.990
hakeshiku natta mune no atsui powaa

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:36.950
From the burning power in my raging heart

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:36.950
sou da minagiru nanika ga

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:40.490
So I'll believe in the present

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:40.490
dakara ima wo shinjite

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:45.660
And start today since it's more than a faint desire

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:45.660
hajimeyou tada no akogare ja nai

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:47.000
Chance for me

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:52.300
Dreams can make even the harshest nightmare pleasant

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:52.300
zankoku na yume ga yume de yume ni narunda

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:56.510
It's just another challenge on the way

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:56.510
hora chousen matteru yo

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:01.430
Where are we headed?

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:01.430
kimi to mukau basho wa doko darou

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:05.180
Into a brilliant hope

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:05.180
mabushii kibou no nake e

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:12.440
Where do we want to go? Let's go find it right now

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:12.440
nozomu basho wa doko darou sagashi ni ikou yo shuppatsu da

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.820
Where we're headed

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.820
mukau basho wa mirai no

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:19.700
is into our hopes for the future

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:19.700
bokura no kibou no naka ni

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:27.040
Our destination is the future, the light is our signal Let's go, go!

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:27.040
nozomu basho wa mirai no kagayaki ga aizu let's go, go

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:35.400
Listen up, Honeys.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.970
For an idol, looking at the camera is the most basic of skills.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:40.970
Give a pose you can be proud of at the moving cameras!

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:41.960
Yes!

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.880
Okay, charming, brilliant!

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.260
Aoi, you're so cool!

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.770
It's harder than I thought. Good luck!

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.020
Thanks!

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.660
I'm ready.

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:04.820
Don't smile <i>at</i> the camera, smile at the other side!

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:07.200
Th-The other side?!

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.170
The only thing on the other side are camera parts...

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.090
That's not what he means by "the other side"...

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:17.380
Good news, Kiriya.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:17.960
Yes?

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.630
You got a fan letter. Aren't you happy?

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:21.840
Huh, a fan letter?

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.580
For me?

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:28.940
Hey, what does it say?

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.900
It says that I looked really cool at my last audition,

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:36.440
and she became my fan 
because of it! It's from a little girl.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:37.570
That's great!

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.040
But I can understand her. You were perfect back then.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.610
All I did was fall on my face.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.580
Don't worry. I'm sure you'll get a fan letter soon.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:50.220
But before that I've got to pass an audition.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.860
Speaking of which...

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:59.010
Information about auditions is posted on this bulletin board. It's pretty useful.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:03.400
"A brand new takoyaki shop, featuring golden octopus: 'Light of the Stars'

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.500
now hiring an advertising mascot."

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:06.760
Sounds fun!

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:11.960
In this sort of personal, local job, you can bring in a lot of excited people to give you support.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.220
It might actually be really useful.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.610
To apply, you'll need to...

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:17.060
Done!

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:17.880
So fast!

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:22.140
Ah, it said it's OK!

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.400
Now I can go in for the audition, right?

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.660
Huh? "Please enter your partner's name"?

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.820
Ichigo, look closely at the application information.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:33.080
"Groups of two"...

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.920
This is a team audition for a pair, you know.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:38.860
A-Aoi...

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:42.170
I know. I'll take the audition with you.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:43.670
Thanks!

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:46.640
Five, six, seven, eight!

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.700
We've got another live audition this time too, huh.

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.660
Just be careful not to fall over again.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:53.640
Ugh, don't say that...

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:56.300
I'm just kidding.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:00.440
I wonder what sort of training I can do in order not to fall again...

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.740
First you need to cultivate your concentration.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.700
Concentration, concentration...

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.440
Next would be strength training, wouldn't it?

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:10.450
Leg strength, huh.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:13.450
One, two, three, four...

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:16.220
Five, six, seven, eight!

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:20.120
I never knew such a nice place was this nearby.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:24.340
Ai-katsu! Ai-katsu! Ai-katsu!

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:42.860
Ouch!

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.760
I can't believe I fell over during my training to avoid just that!

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:48.320
Excuse me, are you alright?

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:55.820
I-I'm fine...

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:59.580
Don't strain yourself.

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:01.700
Want to take a rest over there?

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:02.840
Ah, sure.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:08.340
U-Um, are you...

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:09.340
Yeah?

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:14.060
Hoshimiya Ichigo-chan from Starlight Academy?

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.460
I am, but...

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:21.480
What? No way. Can this be happening?

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:29.610
Does it still hurt?

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:31.860
Thanks, I'm fine!

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:37.870
E-Even if you feel fine now, I think you should still cool it down later.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:41.100
Rest, cooling, and not moving are the best ways to heal.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.700
You sure do know a lot.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:44.380
Because I'm on the track team.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.500
I see.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:50.090
By the way, why do you know my name?

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:53.060
B-Because...

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:54.380
I'm a fan.

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:58.280
Fan? You mean my fan?

00:06:58.280 --> 00:06:59.890
Y-Yeah.

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:03.320
A lot of my friends are Starlight fans,

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:05.400
and I look at the site sometimes too.

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:08.500
Fan... a fan!

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:11.400
This is the first time someone's said they're my fan!

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:14.300
O-Oh...

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:17.410
Probably because you only just recently debuted.

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:20.400
But why me?

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:24.920
I haven't even passed an audition yet.

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:29.080
Still, I think your last audition was really close.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:31.300
Eh?! You saw that?

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:35.260
Yeah. I didn't watch it live, but it was on the Internet.

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:38.520
B-But during it, I really messed up...

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:40.060
It was really lame, right?

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.300
Not at all!

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.780
You got right back up even after falling...

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:47.820
I really admired that.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.820
R-Really?

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:55.860
I've been living in a dorm that's a bit far from here.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:58.600
Same as me. So coincidentally, today...

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:02.400
But you see, I'm not doing well in track,

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.080
and I've gone back to living with my parents.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:10.920
Even though I've done track for so long, I don't have any talent for it.

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:13.930
I was thinking of giving it up soon.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:20.810
But when I watched your video, and saw you get right back up even after falling,

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:23.400
I suddenly got the urge to try running one more time.

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:30.300
I-I never thought that I'd be able to meet you like this.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:31.940
Are you gonna quit track?

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:34.460
W-Well...

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:36.280
When's your next audition?

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:36.950
What's it for?

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:38.780
It's next week.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:41.940
It's only to be an advertising mascot for a takoyaki shop,

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:46.460
but I wanted to train my legs a bit so that I don't fall over like last time.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:48.340
So that's why you're out here?

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:48.960
Yep!

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:51.440
I think that's a great idea.

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:55.090
Y-You'll definitely pass your next audition.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:09:00.060
I hope so too. No, I've got to work hard so that I do pass!

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:05.240
Looks like it was nothing.

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:08.720
Still, you should probably take it easy today.

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:10.360
I will, thanks.

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:12.560
Then, I'll be going.

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:13.360
Ah, wait!

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:16.110
I still haven't heard your name.

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:18.620
Huh? My name's Oota.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:22.040
Oota-kun. You do your best too, okay?

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.540
Y-Yeah. See you!

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:30.240
I'm planning to run tomorrow too, so come join me if you want!

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:50.700
How was your morning run?

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:51.840
Oh, that's right!

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:53.320
Aoi, listen to this!

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:55.440
What? Did something good happen?

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:56.990
Yeah, actually—

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.240
Oh no! We need to hurry, Ichigo!

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:03.320
Huh? Wait! I don't want to run again!

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:08.400
Let's head back, Aoi.

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:11.820
Today's the day that the idol magazines are released, so go on ahead.

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:12.500
Sure.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:15.340
One, two, three, four.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:18.510
Ah, I forgot to tell her about this morning!

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:21.960
I'm back!

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:25.920
You always get so many...

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:28.230
Huh? What's that nice smell?

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:30.240
Oh, this?

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:35.880
Steaming hot takoyaki with special sauce and plenty of spicy mayonnaise on top!

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:39.600
And then there's the dried bonito that appear to come from a dancing angel's feathers fluttering down.

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:40.740
It looks great!

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:43.580
First, we've got to try it out for ourselves.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:47.280
If we pass, we'll get a job where we can have more delicious food like this.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:49.440
Then I guess this counts as practice too!

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:50.250
Exactly right.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:52.560
Have a bite while it's still hot.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:53.500
Sure!

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:55.760
Thanks for the treat!

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:07.020
The outside is crunchy, the inside is creamy, and the octopus is firm and chewy!

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:09.580
A wonderful review from the daughter of a bento shop.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:11.860
Your review of foods can't be matched.

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:16.530
Wow, it's really delicious! {Woah!}

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:20.590
I'm sure I'd win if our audition was for reviewing food...

00:11:20.590 --> 00:11:22.020
The price is reasonable,

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:26.440
and the taste is common, but there's this pleasant gourmet flavor as well...

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:28.540
The image that the maker was aiming for must be...

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:30.920
Aoi's amazing too.

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:35.240
<i>...gives me the strength</i>

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:39.920
<i>to keep fighting.</i>

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:41.480
That went great!

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:44.280
Because of our morning practice, our voices sound a lot better.

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:44.930
That's right!

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:49.280
<i>They're well matched. However...</i>

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:55.600
Oh yeah! I almost forgot, but something good happened this morning. {edited, yo}

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:56.320
What?

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:57.240
You wanna hear?

00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:00.690
You look like you want to tell me. Don't beat around the bush.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.140
Well you know?

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:05.200
I finally got a fan!

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:09.680
While I was running, I met someone who said they're my fan!

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:12.040
Really? That's great!

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.210
You're really becoming more idol-like.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:17.200
Yeah! I was really surprised.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:20.210
They said that they always look at the Starlight Academy website too.

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:22.680
What kind of person? A boy? A girl?

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:26.660
A boy who's about our age, runs track,

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:28.600
and is kind of like a cat.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:31.700
We promised to go running together tomorrow again.

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:34.700
I want to try meeting him too.

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:39.180
Alright, it's decided! I'll go running with you tomorrow too!

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:41.240
Really? Thanks!

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:46.100
He's not here...

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:48.000
Yesterday I saw him at around this time though...

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.000
Ah, it's Oota-kun!

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:56.840
Good morning!

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:58.560
G-Good morning.

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:01.680
I brought my friend with me today.

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:02.760
Nice to meet you.

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:05.760
Kiriya Aoi-chan...

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.340
You know who Aoi is too?

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:13.220
Yeah. A classmate of Ichigo-chan, and known as the Idol Professor.

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:15.500
You sure do know a lot.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:18.270
I have a friend in my club who's a fan of yours.

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:20.520
And so, you're an Ichigo fan?

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:28.160
Amazing, right? I never thought that there would be people cheering us on this close by!

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:30.530
Oh yeah, how's your ankle? Is it better?

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:33.040
Yeah! There's nothing wrong with it.

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:34.910
Take a look.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.290
That's good.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.790
Then let's get running!

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:42.300
I'll match your pace, so feel free to go slowly.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.550
I'm counting on you.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:46.800
But if we do that, won't we disturb your practice?

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:49.050
Well, this is such a rare chance...

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:53.060
Then how about we match our pace with Oota-kun?

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:57.040
I <i>am</i> on the track team, so you two might not...

00:13:57.040 --> 00:13:59.280
But the two of us do Aikatsu, you know.

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:00.060
Huh?

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:03.700
Even idols need strength to be able to sing and dance.

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:06.020
Hey, let's give it a try!

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:08.580
I want to see how long I can keep up!

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:12.580
Got it. Follow me.

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:31.240
<i>Crazy, they're really keeping up with me.</i>

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.180
<i>But it looks like they're reaching their limits...</i>

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:36.900
Should we slow down?

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:38.520
Ichigo...

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.450
I-I can still keep running!

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:26.200
I'm surprised. You were able to keep up until the end.

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:29.220
I'm shocked too.

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:31.360
We're in better shape than you thought, right?

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:33.990
How can you try so hard?

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:39.440
I even said that this would be impossible for an idol.

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:41.250
No, it's not that.

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:44.940
I just wanted to see how far I could get.

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:47.100
Weren't you about to give up halfway?

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:48.760
{Aha! }You noticed?

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:54.260
But isn't it fun to be able to run together like this?

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:55.260
That's right!

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:59.680
It's been a long time since I've had this much fun running.

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:03.120
Are you really going to give up track?

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:06.180
I was going to...

00:16:06.180 --> 00:16:08.060
But I think I'll try a bit longer.

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:09.110
Oota-kun!

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:12.540
When I saw you trying your best to become an idol,

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:16.120
I also somehow got the urge to give it my all too.

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:19.020
I'm even having fun running again!

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:24.660
Your audition was the day after tomorrow, right?

00:16:24.660 --> 00:16:26.880
Yeah, it's a two-person audition with Aoi.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:30.320
I'm going to be in the preliminaries of a local track meet that day too.

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:33.040
I won't be able to see your audition live, but...

00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:34.130
Oota-kun!

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:37.140
Do your best at the meet, okay?

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:39.260
Th-Thank you!

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:41.520
I'll be cheering for you too...

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.100
Thanks!

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:03.310
Oota-kun's track meet should be starting about now.

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:04.290
That's right.

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.100
I hope he wins.

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:07.120
Don't worry.

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:10.080
You're cheering for him with all your heart after all.

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:13.580
Let's focus on our audition.

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:15.640
Even though Oota-kun won't be able to watch,

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:18.940
there are a lot of other people who have come to see us.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:21.600
What's wrong?

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:23.680
I feel like I finally realized something.

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:27.190
The meaning of what Johnny-sensei said during class.

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:31.030
<i>Don't smile </i>at<i> the camera, smile at the other side!</i>

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:34.990
I get it! I need to convey my feelings to the people watching on the other side!

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:37.360
That's the same as when you're on stage.

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:41.180
So if today's audition is for a takoyaki shop...

00:17:42.300 --> 00:17:44.520
Hoshimiya-san, Kiriya-san, please get ready.

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:45.420
Let's go.

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:46.720
Wait a sec, Aoi.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:58.020
I can see it, Ichigo! The takoyaki from back then.

00:17:58.020 --> 00:17:59.880
Open wide, Aoi.

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:04.470
Delicious!

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:06.230
Let's convey these feelings!

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:34.360
Moving on, we have entry number 7, 
Hoshimiya Ichigo and Kiriya Aoi!

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:05.100
And the pair chosen to become the campaign mascots for the golden octopus, "Light of the Stars" is...

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:10.740
Entry number 7, Hoshimiya Ichigo and Kiriya Aoi!

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:13.060
We did it! We passed, Aoi!

00:21:13.060 --> 00:21:15.000
It's my first time passing an audition!

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:16.500
Congratulations, Ichigo!

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:18.500
Yeah, thanks!

00:21:18.850 --> 00:21:21.380
Give these two a round of applause!

00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:28.340
Aoi, a letter came from Oota-kun!

00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:29.500
From Oota-kun?

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:33.460
Ah, a victory sign!

00:21:33.460 --> 00:21:35.280
What's it say?

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:39.180
He set a personal record and was able to pass the preliminaries!

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:42.820
This is thanks to you cheering him on, I'm sure.

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:44.530
Congratulations, Oota-kun.

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:47.530
The two of us passed our auditions as well!

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:52.040
Like this, we were able to try our best because of someone's encouragement,

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:55.500
and in return we were able to get their spirits up.

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:57.040
Idols sure are great!

00:21:57.960 --> 00:22:00.540
Looks like you've come to understand what being an idol is really about!

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:05.050
Ah, does this mean that I've gotten a fan letter now too?

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:08.260
It's yet another anniversary for you to remember!

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:11.140
I even got my very first fan.

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:14.520
That's wrong, Ichigo. 
Oota-kun isn't your first fan.

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:15.890
Huh, why?

00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:18.690
Because your very first fan was me.

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:20.900
R-Really?!

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:22.180
That's right!

00:23:55.420 --> 00:23:57.490
Aoi! Now we've got a fashion show audition!

00:23:57.820 --> 00:23:58.920
Let's do our best together!

00:23:58.920 --> 00:24:01.370
The person you're paired with is <i>that</i> Ran-san!

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:03.320
She's the cool Beautiful Blade!

00:24:03.320 --> 00:24:04.220
What?

00:24:04.220 --> 00:24:05.740
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:05.740 --> 00:24:07.180
Ran! Runway!

00:24:07.180 --> 00:24:09.920
Always passionate, Idol Activities!

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:12.810
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:24:13.920 --> 00:24:15.740
Ai-katsu! Ai-katsu!

00:24:15.740 --> 00:24:17.580
That's nothing like an aphorism!

00:24:17.580 --> 00:24:20.360
Right, that was a cheer, not an aphorism!

00:24:20.360 --> 00:24:21.220
Sensei!

00:24:21.900 --> 00:24:24.900
Don't smile at the camera, smile at the other side, yeah!
